    "created_at": "2016-04-30T05:45:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-30T05:45:53Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the catch. I see two alternatives:\n- (A) the active document of the browsing context of _realm_'s global object (= the Window object on which the interface object of the invoked constructor is found)\n- (B) _realm_'s global object's [newest Document object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#concept-document-window).\n\nThese will differ after navigation: if you saved the `window.HTMLElement` constructor of some iframe, then navigated the iframe, then register `class extends SavedHTMLElement { }` and new it up:\n- (A) will create an element whose node document is the post-navigation document\n- (B) will create an element whose node document is the pre-navigation document\n\nConsistency with `Image` (and presumably `Audio` and other named constructors) probably means it's wisest to go with (A), although to me at least intuitively (B) makes more sense, both in terms of the actual outcome and in terms of it being a shorter path from _realm_.\n\nOpinions @rniwa @annevk @smaug----?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
